---
# Authelia's session store. authelia dials it at session.redis.host=authelia-redis
# (config-secret.yaml.j2), and nothing else does.
#
# THIS POLICY SHIPS WITH THE ROLE THAT NEEDS IT, and that is the whole point of the file's
# location. It lived in roles/k8s/netpol-baseline/ until 2026-09-10, one role away from the
# Deployment whose startup depends on it. `--tags authelia` therefore staged a portal that
# could not reach its session store, and Authelia refuses to start without one: it exits on
# `error initializing session backend: redis connection error: ... i/o timeout` and
# CrashLoopBackOffs behind every forwardAuth route in the fleet. That is issue #1609, and
# `build_k8s_dep_map` cannot see a split like it — it derives a role's edges from templates
# inside that role's own directory, so a dependency expressed in a sibling role produces no
# edge and no ordering constraint to violate.
#
# 6379 is the containerPort AND the Service port — verified 2026-09-10, they match, and
# ansible/tests/services/test_authelia_redis_sessions.py keeps them matching. That test also
# pins this file's co-location, so moving it back fails the suite rather than the pod.
#
# The crowdsec agent sidecar shares the authelia pod, so it arrives here carrying `app:
# authelia` too. That is a property of pod-level identity, not a second rule to write — see
# "A sidecar carries its host pod's network identity" in project memory.
#
# NO `netpol_baseline_enforced` BRANCH, unlike the baseline's own policies. That lever is a
# role default of netpol-baseline, and Ansible role defaults are role-scoped: it does not
# resolve here, and `| default(true)` would read as honouring the lever while ignoring it.
# Dropping it is also the right behaviour rather than a concession. The lever exists to
# restore reachability in a rollback, and the only path that reaches redis at all is the one
# this file grants — so leaving it on cannot be what an operator is rolling back from.
apiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: NetworkPolicy
metadata:
  name: authelia-redis
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
  podSelector:
    matchLabels:
      app: authelia-redis
  policyTypes:
    - Ingress
  ingress:
    - from:
        - podSelector:
            matchLabels:
              app: authelia
      ports:
        - port: 6379
          protocol: TCP
